Identify the real cause of repeated camera correction messages. Resolve competing camera ownership, lifecycle bugs, or other verified causes; do not merely suppress the messages.

Give cutscenes explicit control of the camera and input, with reliable cleanup. Restore the correct camera target, camera mode, movement, cursor behavior, and interaction state after normal completion, skip where supported, interruption, death, respawn, and retry. Prevent overlapping cutscenes and duplicate event handlers.

Test camera framing, clipping, movement, interaction, and control restoration in gameplay and on the train. A cinematic must never leave the player permanently frozen or looking through an abandoned camera.

